# Application-owned state. These configs are rewritten by the program itself
# whenever you change a setting in its TUI, so tracking them guarantees drift:
# every `chezmoi apply` stops on a "has changed since chezmoi last wrote it?"
# prompt, and fails outright in any non-interactive context. Only the app should
# own them.
#
# btop: keep btop.conf untracked, but dot_config/btop/themes/ stays managed so
# the vendored adwaita-dark theme still deploys. btop resolves a bare
# theme name from $HOME/.config/btop/themes, so the theme works without the
# distro shipping it under /usr/share/btop.
**/btop.conf

# OS-specific
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Pi coding agent — secrets (never track API keys)
**/auth.json

# Pi coding agent — sessions are dynamic data tied to working dirs
**/sessions/

# Pi coding agent — local/generated state under ~/.config/pi/agent, not source-of-truth config
# Skills live in ~/.agents/skills/ (synced from dot_agents/skills/). Pi's native
# config dir ~/.pi/agent/skills/ is symlinked to it by dot_config/scripts/run_once_symlink_pi_skills.sh.
.config/pi/agent/bin/
# Pi self-documentation is source-local, not global context for every project.
.config/pi/agent/AGENTS.md
AGENTS.md

# Do not sync nested personal/vendored structures from dot_agents/skills/ to home
.agents/skills/personal/
.agents/skills/vendored/
